		(uuid "3b78ed5e-763a-4870-84d5-144c1937dad9")
	)
	(text_box "Design Factors\n1. Power Supply\n   - 5V (Exact) through a connector\n   - 5V Through USB connector\n   - LDO to create 3V3 for digital domain \n2. Noise in the power supply (especially for CS5381 ADC)\n   - Ferrite beads and capacitors\n   - Maybe low noise LDO for the 3V3\n3. ON/OFF Switch\n   - On the 5V power input\n4. ADA4940 to drive the CS5381 ADC\n   - Amplify output from microphone ICS-40730 by G2.5 for CS5381 full range\n5. Longer traces from microphone ICS-40730 to ADA4940 (about 5cm)\n   - Impedance matching not needed\n   - Length match\n6. ADA4940 close to CS5381\n   - Impeddance matching not needed\n7. Power input polarity protection\n   - Using diode and mosfet\n8. RST Trigger (Low power mode when LOW)\n   - Local RST button\n   - External pin headder input\n9. ADA4940 DISABLE PINS\n  - Active LOW\n  - The DISABLE pin features an internal pull-up network that enables \n    the amplifier for normal operation\n  - DISABLE pin can be left floating (that is, no external connection \n    is required) and does not require an external pull-up resistor to \n    ensure normal on operation\n10. CS5381 ADC sampling at maximum 216kHz\n    - MCLK is 216,000×24×2=10.368 MHz\n    - Will transmit data through FPC ribbon cable"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
